Thats enough for me. That's an extensive list of benefits 


Fear of the Lord is written 14 times in the book of Proverbs and shows up 27 times in Scripture. 

That's not a mistake. The repetition is a signal of importance

If God writes something 27 times it's because he wants us to read it 27 times. Through repetition hes telling us it's important and that we should take it seriously


When people lose reverence and fear of God, they loosen their standards and become more accepting of sin

Fearing the Lord produces obedience

Worldly fear vs holy fear

Fear of God offers us courage and boldness because if we fear God and obey his commandments, we have nothing else to fear

Holy fear produces hatred for sin. Hatred of evil. It also changes our posture toward God. We stop treating him as our friend or magical genie that grants prayers and begin treating him with reverence, awe and humility


Fearing God means having a deep respect, holy reverence,and submission to the Father

It doesnt mean being terrified. 

A holy fear of God serves as a moral compass that guides our daily choices.


It's not by the Love of God that we depart from evil, but by the fear of God

To be righteous is to take obeying God seriously


--> "Fear God and keep His commandments, for this is the the whole duty of man" Ecclesiastes 12:13

Fear God. Obey his commandments. This is our fundamental duty as men.

John Macarthur said: “When God is feared, so is sin. Where there is no fear of God, there is no fear of sin”


Men hold biblical convictions because we love God and we fear God with a holy fear of reverence for his Almighty sovereign power.   


What does it mean to fear God?

It doesn't mean hiding from him like a criminal in the dark, cowering from judgement

Fearing God doesn't mean we live everyday waiting to br struck or beaten

Fearing God means we have finally seen Him as he is. 

We see the Father as holy. Not almost holy. Holy.

We see God as Just. Not mostly just or 99.9% just. Completely and fully just.

We see God as almighty. not impressive. not remarkable. Not exceptional. ALMIGHTY

A Being with complete and total power. Supreme, divine. Almighty. Creator of all things, including us

Having supreme authority, the ability to do all things without limit

And when we finally see God for who He really is. When the creation finally acknowledges the creator with clarity, the heart bows in reverence

That bow. That submission and reverence for the almighty is the fear of the Lord. 






